Informed Consent Form for Multisensory Integration Study
 
We are interested in how people experience emotions when they are presented with a combination of 
sounds and touch stimuli. The study investigates how these two senses interact to shape whether an 
experience feels pleasant, neutral, or unpleasant. Different sounds or textures might give an unpleasant 
experience. These experiences are usually mild and short-lasting. If at any point you feel unwell, please 
inform the researcher immediately. 
